<td>✔️</td>
<td>⚠️<sup>1</sup></td>
<td>⚠️<sup>1</sup></td>
<td>⚠️<sup>1</sup></td>
<td>⚠️<sup>1</sup></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><a href="/en-us/dotnet/api/system.security.cryptography.rsacng" class="no-loc" data-linktype="absolute-path">RSACng</a></td>
<td>✔️</td>
<td>❌</td>
<td>❌</td>
<td>❌</td>
<td>❌</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><a href="/en-us/dotnet/api/system.security.cryptography.rsaopenssl" class="no-loc" data-linktype="absolute-path">RSAOpenSsl</a></td>
<td>❌</td>
<td>✔️</td>
<td>❌<sup>2</sup></td>
<td>❌</td>
<td>❌</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><sup>1</sup> On non-Windows, <a href="/en-us/dotnet/api/system.security.cryptography.rsacryptoserviceprovider" class="no-loc" data-linktype="absolute-path">RSACryptoServiceProvider</a> can be used for compatibility with existing programs. In that case, any method that requires OS interop, such as opening a named key, throws a <a href="/en-us/dotnet/api/system.platformnotsupportedexception" class="no-loc" data-linktype="absolute-path">PlatformNotSupportedException</a>.</p>
<p><sup>2</sup> On macOS, prior to .NET 10, <a href="/en-us/dotnet/api/system.security.cryptography.rsaopenssl" class="no-loc" data-linktype="absolute-path">RSAOpenSsl</a> worked if OpenSSL was installed and an appropriate libcrypto dylib could be found via dynamic library loading. This support was removed in .NET 10.</p>
<h3 id="ecdsa">ECDSA</h3>
