<p><sup>1</sup> Linux distributions don't all have support for the same named curves.</p>
<p><sup>2</sup> Support for named curves was added to Windows CNG in Windows 10. For more information, see <a href="/en-us/windows/win32/seccng/cng-named-elliptic-curves" data-linktype="absolute-path">CNG Named Elliptic Curves</a>. Named curves are not available in earlier versions of Windows, except for three curves in Windows 7.</p>
<p><sup>3</sup> Exporting with explicit curve parameters requires OS library support, which is not available on Apple platforms or earlier versions of Windows.</p>
<p><sup>4</sup> Android support for some curves depends on the Android version. Android distributors may choose to add or remove curves from their Android build as well.</p>
