<h2 id="x509-certificates">X.509 Certificates</h2>
<p>The majority of support for X.509 certificates in .NET comes from OS libraries. To load a certificate into an <a href="/en-us/dotnet/api/system.security.cryptography.x509certificates.x509certificate2" class="no-loc" data-linktype="absolute-path">X509Certificate2</a> or <a href="/en-us/dotnet/api/system.security.cryptography.x509certificates.x509certificate" class="no-loc" data-linktype="absolute-path">X509Certificate</a> instance in .NET, the certificate must be loaded by the underlying OS library.</p>
